From e414696d49521b9ceb7734e037d5aa18ef92d8a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Madalin Bucur <madalin.bucur@nxp.com>
Date: Thu, 31 Oct 2019 16:37:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sdk_dpaa: extend delays in ndo_stop

Make sure all the frames that are in flight have time to be processed
before the interface is completely brought down. Add a missing delay
for the Rx path.

Backport the upstream DPAA stop sequence to the NXP SDK driver's common
stop helper. Its 5-10 ms pre-stop delay can expire with frames still in
flight, after which the MAC is stopped before the FMan port is disabled.
Use the upstream 200 ms drain interval and allow another 200 ms for receive
and completion processing before returning to the caller. The private
interface's NAPI remains enabled until dpa_stop() returns.

This addresses incomplete draining as a possible cause of the FMan busy
warning seen during OpenWrt reboot. Keep the busy checks and warning;
the delay does not establish that a persistent hardware stall recovered.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/linus/e414696d4952]
Signed-off-by: Madalin Bucur <madalin.bucur@nxp.com>
Signed-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>
[tzaman: adapt drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c to the SDK
 common helper in sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_common.c; use _errno return context.]
Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_common.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_common.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_common.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_common.c
@@ -193,7 +193,7 @@
 	/* Allow the Fman (Tx) port to process in-flight frames before we
 	 * try switching it off.
 	 */
-	usleep_range(5000, 10000);
+	msleep(200);
 
 	_errno = mac_dev->stop(mac_dev);
 	if (unlikely(_errno < 0))
@@ -209,6 +209,8 @@
 	if (mac_dev->phy_dev)
 		phy_disconnect(mac_dev->phy_dev);
 	mac_dev->phy_dev = NULL;
+
+	msleep(200);
 
 	return _errno;
 }
